Step 1 — Check your Ubuntu server
lsb_release -a
python3 --version
free -h
df -h /
Step 2 — Install the required packages
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y python3 python3-venv python3-pip
python3 — runs your AI training program.
python3-venv — creates an isolated Python environment.
python3-pip — installs Python libraries.
Step 3 — Create your AI project
mkdir -p ~/ai-first-model
cd ~/ai-first-model
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python --version
which python
Step 4 — Install machine-learning libraries
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install scikit-learn joblib
python -c "import sklearn, joblib; print('scikit-learn:', sklearn.__version__); print('Libraries installed successfully')"
Step 5 — Create your first training program
nano train.py
python train.py


Step 1 — Check your project
cd ~/ai-first-model
source .venv/bin/activate
ls -lh
Step 2 — Create the prediction program
nano predict.py
Step 3 — Run your AI
python predict.py
Step 4 — Understand what's happening
The key distinction is that prediction does not retrain the model. It simply uses the rules learned during training.